% ============================================================================
% ADJ52 case-4 derived rulebook.
% Clinical area: workup of an unexplained multisystem inflammatory illness in
% an older adult whose initial "polymyalgia rheumatica" working diagnosis
% failed on steroids. Differential built from the IR alone (no answer given),
% recursing into subcategories (infection / autoimmune / haematological /
% solid-organ malignancy). Every clause carries a % rationale + source + trust.
%
% adj-lang grammar note: identifiers are /[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*/ (lowercase, no
% leading digit). Magnitudes are encoded QUALITATIVELY (esr(markedly_elevated),
% age(over_50)). LRs are multiplicative (>1 raises, <1 lowers a conclusion).
%
% CORRELATED-EVIDENCE DESIGN: the systemic findings of infective endocarditis
% (new regurgitant murmur, microscopic haematuria from infection-associated
% glomerulonephritis, normocytic anaemia of chronic infection, hypoalbuminaemia,
% low-grade pyrexia, tachycardia, leucocytosis, low-titre ANCA, raised acute-
% phase reactants) are correlated manifestations of ONE bacteraemic immune-
% complex syndrome. They are grouped under a single mechanism directive so the
% combined likelihood ratio fires ONCE and does not double-count / saturate.
% Genuinely orthogonal discriminators (steroid non-response, CT finding,
% absence of fever/night-sweats) are kept as separate contributes.
% ============================================================================

% ===== PRIORS (base rates for a 63yo man with a failed-PMR multisystem illness) =====

% rationale: infective endocarditis is a classic mimic of PMR/vasculitis and is
% the unifying account when a new regurgitant murmur appears with persistent
% inflammation and steroid failure.
prior 0.18 for diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Archives of Rheumatology 2011;26(2): IE presenting as PMR; Merck Manual, Infective Endocarditis" trust authoritative

% rationale: ANCA-associated small-vessel vasculitis is the autoimmune sibling
% raised by haematuria + ANCA + multisystem inflammation.
prior 0.12 for diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "The Rheumatologist, Classification & Diagnosis of GPA; PMC3573492 (ANCA in IE)" trust authoritative

% rationale: PMR is common >50 with girdle pain + raised acute-phase reactants,
% and was the working diagnosis; it remains on the differential.
prior 0.20 for diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "CCJM 2020;87(9):549; EULAR/ACR 2012 PMR criteria" trust authoritative

% rationale: multiple myeloma is a textbook cause of an older adult with back
% pain, very high ESR, normocytic anaemia and weight loss.
prior 0.10 for diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (ESR>100 -> consider myeloma); Geeky Medics PMR differentials" trust authoritative

% rationale: occult solid-organ malignancy can drive constitutional symptoms and
% raised inflammatory markers; a CT was performed to look for it.
prior 0.08 for diagnosis(occult_solid_malignancy)
  source "Medscape, PMR Differential Diagnoses (malignancy mimics)" trust authoritative

% ===== INFECTIVE ENDOCARDITIS =====
% rationale: a NEW loud apical pansystolic murmur radiating to the axilla
% (mitral regurgitation) is the single most specific finding for IE and the
% strongest standalone discriminator here. Kept SEPARATE (not folded into the
% mechanism) because it is the cardinal structural sign.
contributes 8.0 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, Infective Endocarditis (new/changed regurgitant murmur is a major Duke clue); AMBOSS, IE" trust authoritative

% rationale: failure to respond to (and deterioration ON) corticosteroids is a
% key red flag that the illness is infective, not isolated PMR. Orthogonal to
% the bacteraemic-syndrome mechanism, so kept separate.
contributes 3.0 from treatment_response(deterioration_on_steroids) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Archives of Rheumatology 2011;26(2) (lack of steroid response signals IE not PMR)" trust authoritative

% rationale: subacute weight loss / constitutional decline fits the indolent
% bacteraemic course of subacute IE.
contributes 1.6 from symptom(constitutional_weight_loss) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, Infective Endocarditis (constitutional symptoms in subacute IE)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a normal contrast CT with NO malignancy makes occult cancer less
% likely and indirectly supports a non-neoplastic systemic cause such as IE.
contributes 1.3 from imaging(ct_no_malignancy) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Medscape, PMR Differential Diagnoses (negative cross-sectional imaging lowers malignancy)" trust inferred

% mechanism bacteraemic_immune_complex_syndrome for diagnosis(infective_endocarditis) lr 6.0 : lab(esr_markedly_elevated), lab(crp_markedly_elevated), lab(normocytic_anaemia), lab(hypoalbuminaemia), lab(microscopic_haematuria), lab(anca_low_titre), vital(low_grade_pyrexia), vital(tachycardia), lab(leucocytosis_upper)
%   source "Merck Manual + AMBOSS, IE (anaemia, raised ESR/CRP, haematuria/GN, low albumin, fever); PMC3573492 (ANCA positive in 18% of IE)" trust authoritative

% ===== ANCA-ASSOCIATED VASCULITIS (autoimmune sibling) =====
% rationale: microscopic haematuria is a cardinal sign of pauci-immune
% glomerulonephritis in AAV.
contributes 2.5 from lab(microscopic_haematuria) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "The Rheumatologist, Diagnosis of GPA (glomerulonephritis with haematuria)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a WEAKLY positive, LOW-titre ANCA only mildly supports AAV — and is
% well described as a false positive in infective endocarditis. This is the
% discriminator that keeps AAV from running away on the ANCA result alone.
contributes 1.4 from lab(anca_low_titre) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "PMC3573492; PMC4706874 (low-titre ANCA in IE; non-specific at 1:20)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a NEW mitral-regurgitation murmur is NOT a feature of AAV and points
% away from a primary vasculitis toward a structural valvular/infective cause.
contributes 0.4 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "Merck Manual, Infective Endocarditis (valvular murmur is structural/infective, not vasculitic)" trust inferred

% rationale: deterioration ON steroids argues against AAV, which characteristically
% responds to immunosuppression.
contributes 0.5 from treatment_response(deterioration_on_steroids) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "The Rheumatologist, GPA (AAV responds to corticosteroid/immunosuppression)" trust inferred

% ===== POLYMYALGIA RHEUMATICA (the failed working diagnosis) =====
% rationale: shoulder + pelvic girdle pain with stiffness is the cardinal PMR
% distribution.
contributes 3.0 from symptom(girdle_pain_and_stiffness) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "EULAR/ACR 2012 PMR criteria; CCJM 2020;87(9):549" trust authoritative

% rationale: age >=50 is a mandatory PMR entry criterion.
contributes 1.6 from age(over_50) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "EULAR/ACR 2012 PMR criteria (age>=50 required)" trust authoritative

% rationale: raised acute-phase reactants are required laboratory support for PMR.
contributes 1.8 from lab(crp_markedly_elevated) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "EULAR/ACR 2012 PMR criteria; CCJM 2020;87(9):549" trust authoritative

% rationale: PMR responds RAPIDLY and dramatically to low-dose steroids; failure
% to respond (let alone deterioration) is a strong argument AGAINST isolated PMR.
contributes 0.12 from treatment_response(deterioration_on_steroids) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "CCJM 2020;87(9):549; bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (dramatic steroid response expected; reconsider diagnosis if absent)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a NEW regurgitant murmur is not part of PMR and argues against it
% being the whole story.
contributes 0.5 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "CCJM 2020;87(9):549 (PMR is non-structural; new murmur unexplained by PMR)" trust inferred

% rationale: ESR/CRP that climb DESPITE steroids are incompatible with controlled PMR.
contributes 0.3 from lab(crp_rising_on_steroids) to diagnosis(polymyalgia_rheumatica)
  source "What Is Polymyalgia, High CRP in PMR (rising markers on steroids = steroid failure / alternative dx)" trust empirical

% ===== MULTIPLE MYELOMA (haematological mimic) =====
% rationale: an older adult with lower back pain, very high ESR, normocytic
% anaemia and weight loss is a classic myeloma trigger.
contributes 2.2 from symptom(severe_lower_back_pain) to diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (ESR>100 -> myeloma); WebMD Multiple Myeloma (back/rib bone pain)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.8 from lab(esr_markedly_elevated) to diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (very high ESR -> consider myeloma)" trust authoritative
contributes 1.6 from lab(normocytic_anaemia) to diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "PMC4668413 (normocytic normochromic anaemia in myeloma)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a NEW mitral-regurgitation murmur is NOT explained by myeloma; it
% is the discriminator that prevents myeloma from capturing this case on the
% back-pain/ESR/anaemia triad alone.
contributes 0.3 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "WebMD Multiple Myeloma (no valvular murmur in myeloma; murmur unexplained)" trust inferred

% rationale: microscopic haematuria is not a typical myeloma feature (myeloma
% renal disease is cast nephropathy/proteinuria, not haematuria) and renal
% function here is preserved -> mild argument against.
contributes 0.6 from lab(microscopic_haematuria) to diagnosis(multiple_myeloma)
  source "WebMD Multiple Myeloma (myeloma renal disease is proteinuric cast nephropathy, not haematuria)" trust inferred

% ===== OCCULT SOLID MALIGNANCY =====
% rationale: weight loss + constitutional symptoms + raised markers can reflect
% an occult cancer.
contributes 2.0 from symptom(constitutional_weight_loss) to diagnosis(occult_solid_malignancy)
  source "Medscape, PMR Differential Diagnoses (malignancy with constitutional symptoms)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a contrast CT of chest/abdomen/pelvis showing NO malignancy is a
% strong argument AGAINST an occult solid tumour as the cause.
contributes 0.2 from imaging(ct_no_malignancy) to diagnosis(occult_solid_malignancy)
  source "Medscape, PMR Differential Diagnoses (negative CT CAP substantially lowers occult solid cancer)" trust authoritative

% rationale: a new regurgitant murmur is not a generic malignancy feature.
contributes 0.6 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to diagnosis(occult_solid_malignancy)
  source "Merck Manual (new murmur is structural/infective, not paraneoplastic by default)" trust inferred

% ===== NEXT STEP (confirmatory investigation) =====
% rationale: blood cultures (3 sets) + echocardiography are the Duke-criteria
% backbone and the first investigations when a new murmur, fever and embolic /
% immune features appear. This is the recommended next step.
prior 0.25 for next_step(blood_cultures_and_echocardiography)
  source "Merck Manual + AMBOSS, IE (modified Duke criteria: blood cultures + echocardiography first); ESC IE guideline" trust authoritative
contributes 6.0 from exam(new_apical_pansystolic_murmur_radiating_axilla) to next_step(blood_cultures_and_echocardiography)
  source "AMBOSS, IE (new murmur -> TTE within 12h + cultures)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from treatment_response(deterioration_on_steroids) to next_step(blood_cultures_and_echocardiography)
  source "Archives of Rheumatology 2011;26(2) (steroid failure -> hunt for infection / IE)" trust authoritative

% rationale: serum/urine protein electrophoresis + free light chains is the
% confirmatory test if myeloma is being pursued — a competing next step.
prior 0.12 for next_step(serum_protein_electrophoresis_free_light_chains)
  source "bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (ESR>100 -> SPEP/free light chains for myeloma)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.5 from lab(esr_markedly_elevated) to next_step(serum_protein_electrophoresis_free_light_chains)
  source "bpac.org.nz PMR 2023 (very high ESR triggers myeloma screen)" trust authoritative

% rationale: ANCA antigen-specificity (PR3/MPO ELISA) + complement is the test if
% AAV is being pursued — another competing next step.
prior 0.10 for next_step(anca_antigen_specificity_and_complement)
  source "The Rheumatologist, Diagnosis of GPA (PR3/MPO ELISA confirmation)" trust authoritative
contributes 2.0 from lab(microscopic_haematuria) to next_step(anca_antigen_specificity_and_complement)
  source "The Rheumatologist, GPA (haematuria -> confirm vasculitis serology)" trust authoritative

% ===== UNCERTAINTIES (decision-relevant, unresolved) =====
% u3/u4: the ANCA result is the pivotal ambiguity (true small-vessel vasculitis vs
% non-specific low-titre false positive of infective endocarditis). Resolving the
% echo/cultures vs the antigen-specific serology disambiguates IE from AAV.
uncertain { test(echo_vegetation_present), test(blood_cultures_positive), test(echo_no_vegetation_cultures_negative) } for diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, IE (echocardiography + blood cultures adjudicate the diagnosis)"
contributes 9.0 from test(echo_vegetation_present) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, IE (valve vegetation is a major Duke criterion)" trust authoritative
contributes 6.0 from test(blood_cultures_positive) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, IE (typical organism on persistent bacteraemia is a major Duke criterion)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.15 from test(echo_no_vegetation_cultures_negative) to diagnosis(infective_endocarditis)
  source "Merck Manual, IE (negative echo + cultures argues strongly against)" trust authoritative

uncertain { test(anca_high_titre_pr3_mpo_specific), test(anca_remains_low_titre_nonspecific) } for diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "PMC3573492 (antigen-specific high-titre ANCA distinguishes true AAV from IE-associated low-titre ANCA)"
contributes 5.0 from test(anca_high_titre_pr3_mpo_specific) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "The Rheumatologist, GPA (high-titre PR3/MPO-specific ANCA supports AAV)" trust authoritative
contributes 0.5 from test(anca_remains_low_titre_nonspecific) to diagnosis(anca_associated_vasculitis)
  source "PMC4706874 (persistently low-titre non-specific ANCA favours infective cause)" trust authoritative
